+// Pass 2 -- adaptive-support aggregation + winner-take-all. Each candidate's
+// cost is summed over a 9x9 window (every other coarse pixel: ~290 px of the
+// picture at 1/16), each neighbour weighted by how alike its colour is to
+// this pixel's (same surface -> same disparity) and by distance. One noisy
+// descriptor can't decide any more; repetitive texture (panelling, text) is
+// out-voted by the structure around it. This is what made the result depend
+// on the picture's size and position: single-pixel decisions flipped with
+// the downsample grid.
+// Output: .r = dLR (left->right), .g = dRL (right->left), in UV; .ba the
+// matches' uniqueness.
+float4 PSAnaDisp(VSOut i) : SV_Target
+{
+    const int2 p = int2(i.pos.xy);
+    const int W = (int)g_coarseW, Hh = (int)g_coarseH;
+    int Kn, kStep; coarseRange(Kn, kStep);
